g a thriving, close-knit community of quantitative thinkers. Here, traditional disciplinary boundaries blur, and every student's journey is supported by intense peer-to-peer collaboration and deep faculty mentorship.\nGraduate degrees offered:\nM.S. in Mathematics\nPh.D. in Mathematics\nM.S. in Applied Mathematics\nPh.D. in Applied Mathematics\nM.S. in Statistics & Data Science\nCandidates in the master's programs typically complete 30 credit hours.\nPh.D. candidates typically complete the program in 5 - 6 years with additional credit hours (depending on entry level) as well as a dissertation.\nProgram Specific Admissions Requirements\nSubmit a CAS graduate application with supporting materials.\nApplications are accepted for fall enrollment:\nPh.D. apps have a deadline of January 1.\nM.S. apps have a deadline of June 30.\nReady for the Next Step?\nApply to the Mathematics graduate programs via the online graduate application.\nApply Now\nStudent Spotlight\nIsaac Reiter, Ph.D. Student\nIsaac Reiter shares his experience as a Ph.D. student in the College of Arts and Sciences.\nLearn More about Mathematics at Lehigh\nVisit the Department Website\nConnect with Us\nCollege of Arts and Sciences\n9 West Packer Avenue,\nBethlehem,\nPA 18015\nincas@lehigh.edu\n610-758-3300\nFooter Navigation\nUndergraduate\nMajors & Minors\nGet Started\nAcademics\nCurrent Students\nGraduate\nDegrees\nAdmissions\nCurrent Students\nArts\nAlumni\nGO Campaign\nGiving Opportunities\nHow to Make a Gift\nLeadership\nSupport Staff\nConnect with Us\nCollege of Arts and Sciences\n9 West Packer Avenue,\nBethlehem,\nPA 18015\nincas@lehigh.edu\n610-758-3300\nFooter Navigation\nUndergraduate\nMajors & Minors\nGet Started\nAcademics\nCurrent Students\nGraduate\nDegrees\nAdmissions\nCurrent Students\nArts\nAlumni\nGO Campaign\nGiving Opportunities\nHow to Make a Gift\nLeadership\nSupport Staff", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://cas.lehigh.edu/graduate/degrees/mathematics#main-content"], ["Lehigh